WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.186
If you can't add budget, don't add channels.

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:04.896
Across eighty-three brands,

00:00:04.946 --> 00:00:06.063
keeping the same channels with more budget grew about four percent.

00:00:06.113 --> 00:00:08.174
More channels with more budget, about two.

00:00:08.224 --> 00:00:11.747
More channels on a cut fell nearly seven,

00:00:11.797 --> 00:00:13.422
and a big cut,

00:00:13.472 --> 00:00:15.706
about eight.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.850
A retailer facing a budget cut wants TikTok,

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:21.326
podcasts and billboards all at once.

00:00:21.376 --> 00:00:24.958
Spread that thin, and every channel goes quiet.

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:28.636
Better to keep your strongest two or three channels at full weight,

00:00:28.686 --> 00:00:30.346
protect long-lasting TV,

00:00:30.396 --> 00:00:31.549
and stay on air.

00:00:31.599 --> 00:00:33.985
Going dark costs you later.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:40.658
Use it like this: concentrate spend, protect brand channels, and stay consistent.
